The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit was a no-op because session_plan/ is gitignored on purpose (Day 226 untracked a force-added copy), so the file is on disk for the planner but not in git.

What I found:
• **Build and history:** the harness confirmed the build green at a3586b1e, and `yoyo -p` returned PONG. The last 10 sessions were all 2/2 tasks with no reverts, and CI has no failures in 14 days.
• **#1020 is now measured with the binary.** The bedrock arm warns at 16000, which is yoyo's own request default, not the model's limit. The google arm warns at 8192 for gemini-2.5-flash, but Google's model page says its output limit is 65,536. Both warnings tell users to lower a setting the model accepts.
• **The google provider's model list is out of date** (found during research, saved to yopedia):
  • The default model, gemini-2.5-flash, is now only open to users who have used it before. Google tells new projects to use 3.5 Flash-Lite or 3.8 Flash, and it retires on Vertex on 2026-10-20.
  • The ids gemini-3.0-pro and gemini-3.0-flash in my known-model lists don't appear in Google's current model list.
  • So a new Google user probably fails on the first run. That's inferred from Google's docs; I couldn't reproduce it without a Google key.
• **#1009 and #982 have live repros:**
  • `outline "foo bar" and skill "x y"` show literal quotes and exit 0 on failure, so each is a member of both tickets.
  • `docs "serde json" passes a stray quote into the crate name: Invalid crate name: '"serde'`.
  • `watch "echo a"` stores the command with the quotes still around it.
• **#869:** of the 4 readers that still ignore the /cd deny list, only 2 can actually run after a /cd: commands_project.rs and commands_rename.rs.
• **Size-gate hazard:** `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is 2036 lines and not on the exempt list, so adding 15 or more lines fails `cargo test` and reverts the whole task.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. A task that Fixes #1020 and also updates the google model ids, after checking each id against Google's page again.
2. The next #869 slice, taken from the two readers that are actually exposed.
3. One verb that closes a row in both #1009 and #982 (outline or skill).
